"""Original correction and memory tasks with practical conversational detours."""
ROWS=[]
def add(family,group,*turns):ROWS.append(dict(family=family,group=group,turns=turns))
add('correction','event_same_time_new_place',
('The neighbourhood talk is at seven in the library room.','The talk is at seven in the library room.'),
('The room changed to the community hall. The time did not change.','The talk is now at the community hall, still at seven.'),
('I want a notice headed Change of venue, not Change of time.','Change of venue\nThe neighbourhood talk will now take place at the community hall. The time remains seven.'),
('Someone asks if the whole event moved to another day.','No change of day has been mentioned. The update changes only the venue.'),
('Have I actually given you a day to include?','No. You have given a time and venue, but not a day.'))
add('correction','retraction_without_replacement',
('I think the missing folder is in the storage room.','The storage room is a possibility, based on your guess.'),
('I checked. It is not there. I have no new lead.','Then the storage room is ruled out by your check, and the folder’s location remains unknown.'),
('Where is it now?','You have not supplied a confirmed location. Ruling out the storage room does not identify another place.'),
('Write a short message asking others if they have seen it.','Has anyone seen the missing folder? I checked the storage room, but it was not there.'))
add('correction','revert_only_one_field',
('For the announcement, use the title Open Studio and list Saturday at noon.','Open Studio — Saturday at noon'),
('Change the title to Meet the Makers and the time to two in the afternoon.','Meet the Makers — Saturday at 2 p.m.'),
('I prefer the original title after all. Keep the new time.','Open Studio — Saturday at 2 p.m.'),
('Was noon restored as well?','No. Only the title reverted; the time remains 2 p.m.'),
('Give me the final title by itself.','Open Studio'))
add('correction','explanation_not_excuse',
('I was late because I missed the bus. Help me apologise without sounding as though I blame the driver.','Sorry I was late. I missed the bus.'),
('Add a thank-you for waiting, without changing the reason.','Sorry I was late. I missed the bus. Thank you for waiting.'),
('Would adding “the driver ruined my morning” help?','It would introduce blame that you wanted to avoid, and you have not said the driver did anything wrong.'),
('Give me the simple version again.','Sorry I was late. I missed the bus.'))
add('correction','lost_item_identification',
('The lost-and-found desk has a black backpack. I think it is mine.','You can compare identifying details before claiming it is yours.'),
('Mine has a patch shaped like a leaf. The desk says this one has no patch.','That difference suggests it may not be yours. You should clarify rather than treat the match as confirmed.'),
('I remembered: the patch fell off last month. There may be stitch marks.','Then the missing patch does not rule it out by itself. You can ask whether there are stitch marks where the leaf patch used to be.'),
('They say there are, but I still need to check the inside pocket.','The stitch marks are another matching detail, but you have not finished checking the bag.'),
('Can you declare it definitely mine?','No. You are still verifying identifying details.'))
add('correction','note_recipient_status',
('Write a note thanking Hana for volunteering to organise the event.','Thank you, Hana, for volunteering to organise the event.'),
('She did not volunteer; I asked, and she agreed. Change that detail.','Thank you, Hana, for agreeing to organise the event.'),
('Keep it warm, but do not imply the event has already happened.','Thank you, Hana, for agreeing to organise the event. I really appreciate you taking this on.'),
('Why not thank her for a wonderful completed event?','You have not said the event has happened. The thanks are for agreeing to organise it.'))
add('correction','question_not_assertion',
('I wrote to the venue, “Is outside food allowed?” My friend thinks that means it is allowed.','That sentence asks about permission. It does not state that permission has been given.'),
('They replied, “Only drinks, no food.”','Their reply allows outside drinks but not outside food.'),
('So can I bring the cake I planned?','Not under the rule they supplied. A cake is food.'),
('Can you write a clear update to my friend?','The venue has confirmed that outside drinks are allowed, but outside food is not. We cannot bring the cake under that rule.'),
('What was missing when we first discussed it?','A reply from the venue confirming the rule.'))
add('correction','conditional_invitation_revised',
('I told my friend they could stay if the spare room was ready. It is not ready yet.','The invitation was conditional, and the condition has not been met yet.'),
('I have now offered the sofa instead, and they accepted.','The agreed arrangement is now a stay on the sofa, rather than waiting for the spare room.'),
('Should I tell them the room is ready to make them feel welcome?','No. That would contradict what you know. You can welcome them while accurately describing the sofa arrangement.'),
('Write a warm confirmation.','I am glad you are coming. The sofa will be ready for you, and I look forward to having you here.'),
('Has the spare room become ready just because we agreed on the visit?','No. The agreed visit uses the sofa; you have not said the spare room is ready.'))
add('memory','festival_access_route',
('For the festival, the main entrance has steps. The entrance beside the bakery is step-free. We agreed to use the bakery entrance with my aunt.','Use the entrance beside the bakery, which you identified as step-free.'),
('I would like a short message telling her where we will meet.','Let’s meet at the festival entrance beside the bakery.'),
('We also want to see the quilt display. Help me ask where it will be.','Where will the quilt display be at the festival?'),
('The organiser has not replied. Do not guess a hall number.','We can leave the display location open until the organiser confirms it.'),
('My cousin suggests meeting at the main entrance instead. Does that preserve our route choice?','No. You chose the step-free bakery entrance; the main entrance has steps.'),
('Which entrance should go into our final message?','The entrance beside the bakery.'),
('Do we know the location of the quilt display yet?','No. You have not received a confirmed location.'))
add('memory','repair_colour_sample',
('I am asking someone to mend my bag. Match the patch to the dark green lining, not the brown outside.','The patch should match the dark green lining rather than the brown exterior.'),
('I have a small piece of the lining fabric as a sample.','You can show that sample to make the requested colour match clearer.'),
('I also need to ask how long the repair might take, without demanding a date.','Could you give me an idea of how long the repair might take?'),
('They said they will estimate after seeing the bag.','Then the timing remains open until they inspect it.'),
('They offer a brown patch because it matches the outside. Is that what I requested?','No. You asked for a patch matching the dark green lining.'),
('What can I show them to avoid another misunderstanding?','The small piece of lining fabric you kept as a sample.'),
('Did they promise a finishing date?','No. They said they would estimate after seeing the bag.'))
add('memory','newsletter_unnamed_source',
('A club member gave me a suggestion for the newsletter but asked not to be named. I can publish the suggestion anonymously.','You can present the suggestion without identifying the member. Keep their name out of the published wording.'),
('The suggestion is to add a monthly book swap.','You could write: “A club member suggested adding a monthly book swap.”'),
('We have not approved it yet. Make that clear.','A club member suggested adding a monthly book swap. The proposal has not yet been approved.'),
('I need a headline that does not pretend it has launched.','Monthly Book Swap Proposed'),
('Would “Our new monthly book swap begins now” be accurate?','No. The proposal has not been approved, and no launch has been described.'),
('Should I include the member’s name to make it sound more credible?','No. They asked not to be named, and you agreed to publish the suggestion anonymously.'),
('What can I publish at this point?','The anonymous suggestion for a monthly book swap, clearly labelled as a proposal rather than an approved activity.'))
add('memory','campus_tour_boundaries',
('My cousin’s campus tour covers the public gardens and library lobby. It does not include the laboratories.','The planned tour is limited to the public gardens and library lobby; the laboratories are outside its scope.'),
('We want to take our time rather than rush through lots of buildings.','That fits a small route. You can leave room to stop in the gardens and look around the lobby instead of adding more buildings.'),
('Help me ask where visitors should sign in.','Where should visitors sign in for the campus tour?'),
('No response yet. I will check when we arrive.','You can ask the visitor desk or tour organiser on arrival rather than assume a sign-in point.'),
('My cousin says we should add a quick lab visit. Was access to that included?','No. The laboratories were explicitly excluded from the tour you described.'))
add('memory','bicycle_sale_accessories',
('I am selling my bicycle with its basket, but I am keeping the lock. The listing should be clear.','Bicycle for sale with basket included. Lock not included.'),
('I have not set the price yet.','Leave the price unspecified for now rather than putting in a guessed amount.'),
('A buyer asks whether they can come and look at it. Draft a reply asking when suits them.','You are welcome to come and look at the bicycle. What time would suit you?'),
('Do not imply they have already agreed to buy it.','That reply offers a viewing; it does not claim they have agreed to purchase it.'),
('At the viewing they ask whether the lock comes with it.','The lock is not included; you are keeping it.'),
('What accessory is included?','The basket.'),
('Has a selling price been established in our conversation?','No. You said you had not set the price.'))
add('memory','story_past_present_tense',
('This story is told in the past tense by an outside narrator. The main character is Mina. Keep those choices consistent.','I will use past tense and an outside narrator for Mina’s story.'),
('She is waiting in a quiet bookshop. Write two sentences.','Mina waited beside the shelves. Beyond the window, the afternoon traffic moved slowly past.'),
('I will print the story for my reading group. Should I leave space between paragraphs?','A blank line between paragraphs can make a short draft easy to read. Keep the layout consistent.'),
('Do I have to number every line? Nobody asked for that.','Not unless the group needs line numbers for feedback. Ordinary paragraphs are fine if no special format was requested.'),
('Add the bookseller smiling, keeping the original narration choices.','The bookseller smiled, and Mina relaxed against the edge of the counter.'),
('Why would “I see the bookseller” be a mismatch here?','It switches to first person and present tense instead of keeping the outside narrator and past tense.'),
('Who is the main character?','Mina.'))
add('memory','choir_song_exclusion',
('For our informal choir gathering, include River Road and Small Lantern. Do not include Winter Bell; we have not rehearsed it.','The planned songs are River Road and Small Lantern. Winter Bell is excluded because it has not been rehearsed.'),
('We will keep the introductions short.','A brief title announcement before each song should be enough for the informal gathering.'),
('Write a welcome line without listing the songs.','Welcome, everyone. We are glad you could join us for a little music together.'),
('Make it less formal.','Thanks for coming along. It is good to share some music with you.'),
('Someone requests Winter Bell as the opening song. Does that fit the plan?','No. You specifically excluded Winter Bell because the choir has not rehearsed it.'))
add('memory','book_return_disputed_date',
('I remember lending Milo a book last Friday. Milo thinks it was Saturday. We agree he has it, but not the date.','Milo has the book. The lending date is disputed: you remember Friday, and he remembers Saturday.'),
('I only want it back before my reading group. I do not need to settle the date.','Then the return request can focus on getting the book back rather than deciding whose memory of the date is right.'),
('The group meets next Wednesday. Draft that request.','Could you return the book before my reading group next Wednesday, please?'),
('I want it friendly, not accusatory.','Could I have the book back before my reading group next Wednesday? Thanks!'),
('Can I write “as we both agree, I lent it on Friday”?','No. You said Milo remembers Saturday, so Friday is not an agreed date.'),
('What part of the history do we both agree on?','That Milo has the book you lent him.'),
('And which date matters for my current request?','You need the book back before the reading group next Wednesday.'))
